    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">HLD</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">LLD</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">Flipkart</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">Amazon</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">Microsoft</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">Uber</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">Walmart</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>HLD vs LLD: Handling Combined Design Rounds</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Indian SDE-2 loops almost always have two kinds of design round: boxes-and-arrows HLD, and class-level LLD or machine coding. This page shows what each one tests, how to run a 90-minute machine-coding round, the few principles and patterns that matter, and outline answers for the four classic problems.</p>\n      ",
